ousand is “a bit more than a thousand” underestimates the scale. Correction: 10 thousands; 100 hundreds. Why: the correction restores accurate use of ten thousand.","type":"short_answer"}],"resources":null,"response_prompt":"Include your independent working and reflection, with reasons where requested.","review_status":"unreviewed","seed_key":"s2-mat-y4-w04-l3","sort_activity":null,"source_note":"Proposed Stage 2 NESA mathematics alignment using verified outcome code wording where recorded in lesson-pipeline/sources; content-point mapping remains pending.","spelling":null,"spelling_focus":null,"stage":"S2","stage_hints":{"accept":["Today you will practise ten thousand.","Read the mission before you start calculating.","Keep the place or unit you are working with in view."],"guided":["Attempt the guided prompt without looking ahead.","Afterwards, compare your working with the feedback.","Adjust anything that does not match the method."],"learn":["Study how the first demonstration is built.","Point to the place or distance that carries the method.","Then write the reason without copying every sentence."],"quiz":["Read every option before you choose.","Eliminate answers that ignore place value or working.","Prefer accurate method over a guess that merely looks neat."],"submit":["Confirm that your working and reason are both present.","Proofread digits, places and operation signs.","Make sure the final evidence matches the lesson purpose."],"teach0":["Read the stage title and find the worked model.","Name one exact place, value or distance before you decide.","Try the small prompt before opening the comparison."],"teach1":["Return to the model and list the key numbers.","Say what each number represents in the method.","A final answer alone is weaker than labelled working."],"teach2":["Compare a weak attempt with stronger working.","Change the value or method, not only how neat it looks.","Name the mistake you are repairing."],"teach3":["Choose fresh numbers that still use the same skill.","Write one reason in your own words.","Do not retype the worked model as your answer."],"write":["Follow every part of the independent instructions.","Include original working and a short reason.","Save work that shows the skill on new numbers."]},"subject":"Number and Algebra","success_criteria":["I can use ten thousand with a specific example from this lesson.","I can identify investigate and explain why it matters.","I can practise model independently on a new prompt.","I can notice scale needs and correct a likely mistake."],"suspense_builder":null,"teach_steps":[{"check":{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Investigating how big ten thousand is means building a model or count structure (hundreds of hundreds) so the quantity is not just a digit string. Supported working follows the actual numbers and purpose of the task.","options":["A guess with no working.","Investigating how big ten thousand is means building a model or count structure (hundreds of hundreds) so the quantity is not just a digit string.","A calculation unrelated to the numbers given.","An answer copied without understanding."],"question":"Which choice best shows accurate use of this idea about ten thousand?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\n100 hundreds = 10,000. A grid of 100 dots, copied 100 times, models ten thousand. Relating 10,000 to 1,000 (ten thousands) supports scale sense.\n\nTRY FIRST\nHow many thousands make ten thousand? How many hundreds?\n\nFEEDBACK\n10 thousands; 100 hundreds.","explain":"Investigating how big ten thousand is means building a model or count structure (hundreds of hundreds) so the quantity is not just a digit string.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner choose methods based on place value, quantity and accurate working, rather than guessing digits by shape alone. Keep every step justified.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the places, values or distances that carry the method. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your working with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your reasoning? If a digit or place is uncertain, identify what would have to be regrouped or counted again. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Thinking ten thousand is “a bit more than a thousand” underestimates the scale. Correct the value or method, not just the appearance of the digits.","title":"Understand and model","visual":[{"alt":"Model for the size of ten thousand.","caption":"Build groups, not only digits.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Model</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">100 hundreds = 10,000</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Scale</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">10 × 1,000</text></g></svg>"}],"visual_before":[{"episode":{"scenes":[{"bg":"room","lines":[{"text":"I can see the example, but I am not sure which number or place matters most.","who":"pip"},{"text":"Name the places, values or distances that carry the method before you decide.","who":"juno"},{"text":"I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.","who":"pip"},{"pause_after":true,"text":"Pause here. Use this model: 100 hundreds = 10,000. A grid of 100 dots, copied 100 times, models ten thousand. Relating 10,000 to 1,000 (ten thousand Then write your own working.","who":"juno"}]}],"title":"Talk through the first model","transcript":"Pip: I can see the example, but I am not sure which number or place matters most.\nJuno: Name the places, values or distances that carry the method before you decide.\nPip: I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.\nJuno: Pause here. Use t